AstraOS is an independent Linux distribution based on Debian GNU/Linux.
It is not an official Debian release and it is not yet a stable product.
This is an ALPHA release: expect defects. See /usr/share/doc/astraos/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md

Useful commands
  astraos-info              OS, kernel, hardware and network summary
  astraos-info --json       the same summary, machine readable
  astraos-help              where to find documentation and how to report problems
  astraos-welcome           first-run guidance (installed systems)

Live session
  This is a LIVE environment. It is running from the installation medium.
  Changes made here are NOT saved to disk and will be lost when you reboot.
  To keep anything, install AstraOS with the installer.

  The live user has administrative rights through sudo. The root account is locked.

